WEBVTT

00:00.540 --> 00:02.450
HARUMOTO STORE
Where is Yuki's sister now?

00:02.800 --> 00:03.840
I don't know.

00:03.840 --> 00:04.680
Ah?

00:04.680 --> 00:07.000
You don't know and yet you still
dare to ask me to treat you to ramen.

00:07.000 --> 00:10.760
The act of inquiring information
from me is worth a bowl of ramen.

00:10.960 --> 00:14.220
And you only have the clues
of a bell and the name Hua, right?

00:14.440 --> 00:16.380
I'll do as much as
this bowl of ramen costs.

00:16.540 --> 00:17.960
I'm going to start.

00:18.400 --> 00:21.080
As a teacher, how dare you
let a student treat you.

00:21.780 --> 00:24.640
Don't talk to me while I'm eating ramen.

00:31.840 --> 00:36.240
Authentic Japanese noodles
really have a distinctive taste.

00:36.240 --> 00:37.880
Even better than sushi.

00:37.880 --> 00:40.280
Maybe that's 80% of the reason
I'm staying in Japan.

00:40.280 --> 00:41.400
That's so high.

00:41.600 --> 00:43.640
Yuki, you must understand me, right?

00:47.060 --> 00:47.960
You!

00:48.640 --> 00:50.400
You!

00:50.880 --> 00:52.740
Don't put on that happy face.

00:52.740 --> 00:55.700
I know you love katsuta sauce.

00:56.120 --> 00:58.720
But I didn't expect you
to carry a bottle with you.

00:58.720 --> 01:02.080
Alright. To her, it's like
we want to add much garlic.

01:02.080 --> 01:04.000
Apologize to the ramen.

01:04.000 --> 01:07.080
If you want to inquire information from me,
don't put in sauce next time we eat ramen.

01:07.080 --> 01:08.600
That's my deal.

01:08.600 --> 01:10.840
There's not much sauce left.

01:13.920 --> 01:20.300
(You Are Ms. Servant.)

02:41.651 --> 02:43.171
KATSUTA DELI
Sorry.

02:43.360 --> 02:45.680
(Episode 8: Autumn Appetite with You)
All the sauce has been sold out.

02:47.020 --> 02:51.080
The students bought many bottles.

02:51.080 --> 02:52.179
I see.

02:52.180 --> 02:54.100
Because the Katsuta's Festivals
are coming up soon.

02:54.100 --> 02:56.300
I'm really sorry, Miss Maid.

02:56.300 --> 02:59.980
During this time,
the sauce is just in too high demand.

02:59.980 --> 03:02.220
There are also a bunch
of orders to handle.

03:02.220 --> 03:05.620
You can buy it after a week.

03:05.620 --> 03:06.820
A week?

03:06.820 --> 03:08.380
I'm sorry.

03:11.400 --> 03:12.260
Not at all.

03:12.960 --> 03:16.680
Thank you for always
making such a delicious sauce.

03:17.880 --> 03:20.420
This is the most obvious growth
in her so far.

03:21.820 --> 03:22.940
Hmm.

03:23.460 --> 03:26.480
There's only this little left.
Looks like it won't last a week.

03:26.720 --> 03:29.540
I-I will cherish it.

03:29.940 --> 03:32.380
I need to talk about something else
to cheer her up.

03:32.820 --> 03:34.620
Well.

03:34.620 --> 03:36.340
about your sister.

03:36.340 --> 03:38.580
What would you say to her
if you saw her again?

03:39.660 --> 03:40.780
Actually,

03:41.360 --> 03:44.240
I have very vague memories of my youth.

03:44.700 --> 03:46.880
I don't even remember
what my sister looks like clearly.

03:47.160 --> 03:50.520
Even the memory of my parents
are fragmentary.

03:51.300 --> 03:53.360
By the time I noticed, I was all alone.

03:54.180 --> 03:56.980
But this bell
is the only thing I remember.

03:58.320 --> 04:01.720
This is the bell that my mom
gave to my sister and me.

04:02.500 --> 04:06.380
I thought if I kept it with me,
maybe one day my sister would find me.

04:07.120 --> 04:08.560
However, over these ten years,

04:08.900 --> 04:11.120
the miracle I hoped for did not happen.

04:12.540 --> 04:13.500
Moreover,

04:13.500 --> 04:15.620
I'm actually scared to see her again.

04:16.140 --> 04:20.620
Maybe my sister's been living
with a grudge against me.

04:20.880 --> 04:21.640
Eh?

04:22.000 --> 04:25.180
So, am I being nosy to ask Miss Grace
to help in searching for her?

04:25.360 --> 04:27.600
No, not at all.

04:28.160 --> 04:29.720
Even if I never meet her again,

04:30.080 --> 04:32.160
knowing that my sister is safe and sound

04:32.340 --> 04:34.580
would make me feel relieved.

04:35.360 --> 04:36.480
I see.

04:38.820 --> 04:42.760
I was trying to cheer her up,
but instead she comforted me.

04:42.760 --> 04:43.940
Hello, you two.

04:44.100 --> 04:46.020
So, you have a sister, Miss Yuki.

04:46.220 --> 04:49.020
She must be a beauty like you, Miss Yuki.

04:49.360 --> 04:50.940
Taiga, Kobachi.

04:51.160 --> 04:52.980
What are you doing here?

04:53.320 --> 04:54.420
Hey, hey.

04:54.420 --> 04:56.800
Today is the release day
for Nazca's new song.

04:57.040 --> 04:57.920
Moreover,

04:57.920 --> 05:01.120
I even got this limited signed edition.

05:01.480 --> 05:03.880
God, thank you.

05:03.880 --> 05:06.900
Is Nazca the singer who'll participate in
this year's Katsuta's Festivals?

05:07.240 --> 05:08.060
Yes.

05:08.220 --> 05:09.800
Hitoyoshi, are you going shopping?

05:10.060 --> 05:13.260
You two have a nice relationship.

05:13.580 --> 05:14.360
Eh?

05:14.360 --> 05:16.460
A cousin and a relative.

05:16.760 --> 05:20.220
You've been surrounded
by many blood relatives lately.

05:20.500 --> 05:22.220
It's all coincidence.

05:22.220 --> 05:24.160
You don't hang out with us anymore.

05:24.160 --> 05:27.100
Alright, Kobachi, don't be jealous.

05:27.760 --> 05:29.680
I'm really grateful to you, Miss Yuki.

05:30.060 --> 05:33.160
Since you are here, Hitoyoshi seems happy.

05:33.940 --> 05:35.180
Master Hitoyoshi…

05:35.480 --> 05:36.860
Right.

05:36.860 --> 05:39.480
Hitoyoshi during his junior high years
was pretty terrible.

05:39.480 --> 05:41.880
It's a secret only those
who went to school with him would know.

05:41.880 --> 05:43.500
That…

05:43.500 --> 05:46.300
At that time, he was
in his rebellious period against his dad,

05:46.300 --> 05:48.740
and also suffering from Chuunibyou.

05:49.520 --> 05:50.620
Chuunibyou?

05:50.820 --> 05:53.900
I remember him wearing a coat
on a hot summer day.

05:53.900 --> 05:55.480
SUN
His nickname at that time was Rage Knife.

05:55.480 --> 05:56.710
Ah!

05:56.920 --> 05:58.480
Rage Knife.

05:59.640 --> 06:02.220
This is on a whole different level
from Miss Yuki's dark history.

06:02.220 --> 06:03.980
I feel so embarrassed.

06:03.980 --> 06:07.700
And do you know the reason
why he doesn't clean the house?

06:07.700 --> 06:10.400
He can do it, but the reason
he doesn't clean is really childish.

06:10.400 --> 06:11.380
Ah!

06:11.380 --> 06:13.960
Taiga, stop it.

06:15.320 --> 06:16.060
Ah!

06:16.060 --> 06:19.620
My signed CD!

06:30.200 --> 06:31.780
KATSUTA SAUCE

06:35.990 --> 06:38.450
END

06:39.910 --> 06:41.500
THAT NIGHT

06:43.500 --> 06:45.710
KATSUTA SAUCE

06:45.900 --> 06:47.720
I'm so sad.

06:48.040 --> 06:51.320
I can't believe you treat me like this.

06:51.320 --> 06:52.960
S-Sorry.

06:52.960 --> 06:56.260
From now on, don't come to me again.

06:59.000 --> 07:00.900
Miss Yuki, may I come in?

07:01.120 --> 07:01.880
Ah!

07:02.160 --> 07:03.600
Okay.

07:03.600 --> 07:04.560
Come in.

07:05.840 --> 07:07.600
You just woke up?

07:07.960 --> 07:09.440
It's already noon.

07:10.100 --> 07:13.460
I-I'm disliked by Katsuta sauce.

07:13.860 --> 07:15.240
I can't do it anymore.

07:15.580 --> 07:18.540
I have nothing left to live for.

07:18.880 --> 07:20.660
Tell me the details.

07:22.540 --> 07:23.680
I see.

07:23.900 --> 07:26.480
Mr. Katsuta sauce said that
to you in a dream.

07:26.900 --> 07:28.600
Don't care about it so much.

07:28.600 --> 07:31.120
You can buy it next week.

07:31.380 --> 07:32.340
That's right.

07:32.560 --> 07:34.120
Although that's part of the reason,

07:34.380 --> 07:36.540
it's not the only thing I dreamt about.

07:37.120 --> 07:37.880
What?

07:38.160 --> 07:40.040
Did you have other scary dreams?

07:40.540 --> 07:41.520
Nothing.

07:49.860 --> 07:50.860
THE NEXT DAY

07:50.860 --> 07:52.260
I'm sorry.

07:52.820 --> 07:55.320
ANOTHER DAY LATER

08:00.320 --> 08:01.240
Come in.

08:02.440 --> 08:06.380
C-Can you sleep with me?

08:06.380 --> 08:07.160
Eh?

08:07.380 --> 08:09.540
S-She's asking for help?

08:09.880 --> 08:11.640
I'm afraid to sleep.

08:12.100 --> 08:14.020
And I'm so afraid
that I can't fall asleep.

08:14.440 --> 08:17.220
Let's set aside
the matter of sleeping together,

08:17.960 --> 08:22.279
there's an exam tomorrow,
so I've decided to stay up and study.

08:22.280 --> 08:25.120
I can talk to you until you want to sleep.

08:25.720 --> 08:28.100
Is that really okay?

08:29.920 --> 08:30.800
Hmm.

08:41.080 --> 08:42.640
Master Hitoyoshi.

08:44.180 --> 08:47.680
You are really gentle and caring
towards the people around you.

08:48.140 --> 08:50.640
You are a man of great character.

08:50.900 --> 08:52.740
Why bring this up?

08:53.120 --> 08:54.920
That's not the case.

08:55.580 --> 08:56.919
Well…

08:56.920 --> 09:01.740
For a person like you,
have you ever disliked anyone?

09:02.160 --> 09:03.140
Dislike?

09:03.820 --> 09:05.520
Dislike.

09:05.960 --> 09:09.060
There isn't someone I truly dislike
from the bottom of my heart.

09:09.520 --> 09:11.340
But if I had to name one,

09:13.020 --> 09:14.380
it would be my father.

09:14.820 --> 09:15.840
Your father?

09:16.420 --> 09:18.600
Rather than dislike,

09:18.900 --> 09:20.740
since many things happened in the past,

09:21.000 --> 09:23.420
so I try to keep distance from him.

09:23.760 --> 09:26.060
It's an inevitable part
of family relationships.

09:27.160 --> 09:29.840
Inevitable part of family relationships?

09:30.480 --> 09:32.560
I dislike you the most.

09:37.060 --> 09:38.080
Miss Yuki?

09:44.660 --> 09:49.020
Well, I think if I stay here,
I would probably disturb your studying.

09:49.300 --> 09:51.760
I'd better go back to my room.

09:52.260 --> 09:53.660
Is that so?

10:04.620 --> 10:06.519
KATSUTA SAUCE
It's all your fault.

10:06.520 --> 10:08.599
KATSUTA SAUCE
It's all your fault.

10:08.600 --> 10:11.500
KATSUTA SAUCE
Not only did you abandon me, but also your sister.

10:11.740 --> 10:14.339
You are good for nothing except killing.

10:14.340 --> 10:16.400
That's why everyone dislikes you.

10:17.060 --> 10:18.480
That's not true.

10:19.260 --> 10:21.039
I've always been working hard

10:21.040 --> 10:22.080
to be an ordinary girl.

10:22.080 --> 10:25.620
Even now, you keep causing trouble
for Hitoyoshi and others.

10:26.160 --> 10:27.739
Just look.

10:27.740 --> 10:31.100
They don't want to be around
someone like you at all.

10:31.340 --> 10:35.320
Everything that's happened so far
is all your fault.

10:37.500 --> 10:39.699
How old are you now, Maria?

10:39.700 --> 10:42.140
I'll be seven on the 25th of next month.

10:42.440 --> 10:45.160
I heard you can speak fifteen languages.

10:45.160 --> 10:46.040
Yes.

10:46.040 --> 10:48.340
I learned them
because I wanted to help my mom.

10:48.340 --> 10:51.240
As a child, you were hailed as a prodigy.

10:51.240 --> 10:54.360
I hear your mom
works as an interpreter, right?

10:54.600 --> 10:55.380
Yes.

10:55.380 --> 10:58.759
You are very polite.

10:58.760 --> 11:01.680
It must be because of
your mom's good upbringing, isn't it?

11:01.680 --> 11:02.620
Yes.

11:02.620 --> 11:05.100
My mom is very beautiful and smart,

11:05.100 --> 11:06.360
and with a pretty smile.

11:06.360 --> 11:10.980
You have excellent observation skills,
a photographic memory,

11:10.980 --> 11:13.919
and motor nerves far beyond
those of young children.

11:13.920 --> 11:16.060
You were very popular,

11:16.060 --> 11:20.399
but you had no interest in
being talented or on the world stage.

11:20.400 --> 11:23.800
The only thing you were interested in…

11:24.640 --> 11:26.440
Mom, Dad.

11:28.780 --> 11:31.980
Seeing your beloved parents' happy smiles.

11:34.260 --> 11:38.260
Happy birthday to you,

11:40.260 --> 11:42.440
Maria, happy birthday.

11:45.580 --> 11:46.860
You've got it on your face.

11:53.100 --> 11:54.479
Is it a guest?

11:54.480 --> 11:55.860
I'll go take a look.

11:55.860 --> 11:57.039
I'll go too.

11:57.040 --> 11:59.380
Maria, you go ahead and eat.

12:07.040 --> 12:07.820
No.

12:08.160 --> 12:09.520
No way.

12:27.980 --> 12:29.200
Don't go.

12:30.000 --> 12:30.820
Mom,

12:31.200 --> 12:32.060
Dad.

12:32.760 --> 12:34.212
Don't go!

12:34.560 --> 12:36.005
Stay here.

12:36.900 --> 12:39.040
It's all my fault.

12:39.560 --> 12:40.960
I'm sorry.

12:41.320 --> 12:42.999
I'm sorry.

12:43.000 --> 12:47.479
In order to capture you,
your parents got killed,

12:47.480 --> 12:50.040
and your sister was involved.

12:50.460 --> 12:54.100
Losing loved ones
makes you lose your feelings.

12:54.420 --> 12:59.480
That obsession transferred the love
for your parents onto your sister.

13:00.520 --> 13:01.400
Why?

13:01.960 --> 13:04.200
Why did you do so?

13:04.720 --> 13:05.500
No!

13:05.720 --> 13:07.300
I dislike you the most.

13:07.600 --> 13:09.040
I don't want this bell.

13:16.840 --> 13:18.920
You were finally rejected by your sister.

13:18.920 --> 13:23.180
Your only option is to assassin.

13:24.140 --> 13:26.679
Killing to stay alive.

13:26.680 --> 13:29.696
At some point,
you started living for killing.

13:30.140 --> 13:34.320
You've become the most vicious assassin.

13:42.660 --> 13:44.407
Welcome back, Yuki.

13:45.080 --> 13:47.618
My beloved disciple.

13:50.280 --> 13:51.080
Miss…

13:51.320 --> 13:52.180
Miss Yuki.

13:56.440 --> 13:57.360
Are you okay?

13:58.320 --> 13:59.180
Ah!

13:59.760 --> 14:01.799
Master Hitoyoshi.

14:02.260 --> 14:04.344
Sorry, I ran into your room.

14:04.960 --> 14:07.860
Because you looked weird just now,
I came over to check on you.

14:10.480 --> 14:12.439
You've been moaning.

14:12.440 --> 14:13.436
Are you okay?

14:22.040 --> 14:22.780
Oh.

14:22.780 --> 14:24.420
Oh.

14:25.660 --> 14:27.992
Miss Yuki.

14:32.180 --> 14:35.333
I understand
that I am causing you trouble.

14:35.800 --> 14:37.585
But now,

14:40.680 --> 14:42.479
please let me

14:42.480 --> 14:44.592
do this just for a moment.

14:46.140 --> 14:47.345
Miss Yuki?

14:53.900 --> 14:56.187
Did you have a nightmare again?

14:57.420 --> 15:00.900
It might be a nightmare,

15:01.860 --> 15:04.529
but it's not just that.

15:05.640 --> 15:06.697
It was a dream

15:07.400 --> 15:09.408
from my distant past.

15:10.480 --> 15:13.830
Sorry, I don't remember anything.

15:15.060 --> 15:16.374
I see.

15:21.900 --> 15:23.359
Just like this,

15:23.360 --> 15:25.999
patting a baby's back gently
will stop their crying.

15:26.000 --> 15:29.240
They say it's because
it sounds like a mother's heartbeat,

15:29.240 --> 15:30.740
it comforts them when they hear it.

15:31.280 --> 15:34.060
That's what my mom told me.

15:38.840 --> 15:41.000
The sound of Master Hitoyoshi's heartbeat

15:41.820 --> 15:43.734
is very comforting

15:53.300 --> 15:54.050
SCIENCE CLASSROOM
Eh?

15:54.300 --> 15:56.520
Yuki, don't you know
what Katsuta's Festivals are?

15:57.080 --> 15:58.439
Right.

15:58.440 --> 16:01.799
I wondered
if they're some kind of celebration.

16:01.800 --> 16:02.840
You're right.

16:03.160 --> 16:05.799
Its formal name
is Katsuta's Three Great Festivals,

16:05.800 --> 16:09.220
including Sports Festival,
Cultural Festival and Music Festival,

16:09.220 --> 16:10.880
commonly referred to
as Katsuta's Festivals.

16:10.880 --> 16:12.730
It is a traditional event

16:12.730 --> 16:13.660
KATSUTA'S FESTIVALS
of Ogiso high school.

16:13.860 --> 16:15.720
We take the class as a unit
to participate in the event

16:15.720 --> 16:19.059
to strive for the comprehensive ranking
of the three great festivals.

16:19.060 --> 16:21.519
And the prize for the winning class

16:21.520 --> 16:24.660
is said to be the special katsuta sauce.

16:24.660 --> 16:26.300
It's commonly called Katsuta Special.

16:27.360 --> 16:30.040
For Miss Yuki who has no sauce to savor,
this is a cruel topic.

16:30.260 --> 16:31.260
However,

16:31.260 --> 16:33.220
for first-year students
unfamiliar with Katsuta's Festivals,

16:33.220 --> 16:35.019
it's impossible to win.

16:35.020 --> 16:37.400
It must be
the Student President's class that wins.

16:37.560 --> 16:41.479
If one wants to win,
then has to win in the Cultural Festival.

16:41.480 --> 16:43.300
So as the grades.

16:43.680 --> 16:44.780
Grades matter too?

16:44.980 --> 16:45.900
Right.

16:45.900 --> 16:47.430
Miss Yuki, how did you do on the test?

16:47.900 --> 16:49.880
YUKI YOKOYA, 42 SCORES
A passing grade.

16:49.880 --> 16:50.940
YUKI YOKOYA, 42 SCORES
What a big smile.

16:51.260 --> 16:53.980
I think I at least need to dodge
the after-school tutoring.

16:53.980 --> 16:56.219
It's really great you didn't fail.

16:56.220 --> 16:58.820
After all, grades will affect
the grading of Katsuta's Festivals.

16:58.820 --> 16:59.840
Grading?

17:00.060 --> 17:02.438
EACH TERM'S FINAL GRADES
The average class score will also count

17:02.438 --> 17:05.228
THE RANKING OF SCORES IN THE THREE GREAT FESTIVALS
as a comprehensive ranking for Katsuta's Festivals.

17:05.480 --> 17:08.820
I remember our class average
is around 60 scores.

17:09.094 --> 17:10.617
The failing score is 37.

17:10.618 --> 17:12.670
-Eh?
-Those who don't reach this score will lose the right to compete.

17:12.670 --> 17:15.090
YUKI YOKOYA, 42 SCORES

17:15.180 --> 17:18.519
That means if my score
is below average, I will…

17:18.520 --> 17:20.040
What should I do?

17:20.040 --> 17:21.540
I-It's okay.

17:21.540 --> 17:24.640
As long as you don't fail,
the difference in scores won't be too big,

17:24.640 --> 17:26.840
and you won't be deprived
of the right to compete.

17:26.840 --> 17:28.160
People with poor test scores

17:28.160 --> 17:30.220
need to do well in the practical subject.

17:30.500 --> 17:31.740
Do well

17:32.480 --> 17:33.552
in the practical subject.

17:34.320 --> 17:36.514
Do well in the practical subject.

17:36.980 --> 17:39.839
I remember last year was a riddle contest.

17:39.840 --> 17:41.686
I wonder what it will be this year.

17:47.800 --> 17:50.560
This time, the stock
of Katsuta Bread is very limited.

17:50.560 --> 17:53.100
I went through a lot of trouble to get it.

17:53.100 --> 17:55.760
You should thank me, Sauce Junkie.

17:55.940 --> 17:57.939
Hmm, thank you very much.

17:57.940 --> 17:59.540
Thank you, Grace.

18:01.240 --> 18:02.360
What's wrong?

18:02.360 --> 18:04.140
Nothing.

18:05.040 --> 18:08.600
Did she forget that I had previously
taken Hitoyoshi as a hostage?

18:08.600 --> 18:10.840
Or did she never care about me at all?

18:11.540 --> 18:13.760
Take the stuff and disappear.

18:13.760 --> 18:16.499
It would be very dangerous
if someone saw us making a deal here.

18:16.500 --> 18:17.779
What?

18:17.780 --> 18:20.180
We're not engaging in
any black market dealings.

18:20.180 --> 18:22.560
Anyway, just go.

18:22.560 --> 18:26.500
I need to finalize the test scores
before the fifth period PE class.

18:28.300 --> 18:29.639
Master Hitoyoshi.

18:29.640 --> 18:33.139
About the Katsuta's Festivals
you mentioned,

18:33.140 --> 18:37.640
what kind of grades
do our class need to win?

18:37.640 --> 18:39.920
D-Do you really want to win?

18:39.920 --> 18:43.799
Indeed. With your skills,
it would be possible.

18:43.800 --> 18:46.560
But be careful not to do anything
that would expose your identity.

18:46.560 --> 18:49.180
Yuki, do you want
to participate in Katsuta's Festivals?

18:50.080 --> 18:53.080
But you didn't write your name
on the PE written test,

18:53.080 --> 18:54.680
so it's considered a fail,
and you can't compete.

18:56.800 --> 18:59.240
During the test, I peeked at your answers.

18:59.420 --> 19:01.680
NAME
You were the only one who didn't write a name.

19:01.680 --> 19:04.160
NAME
I think this must be your paper.

19:04.320 --> 19:06.400
What a pity!

19:06.400 --> 19:09.159
In terms of scores, you didn't fail.

19:09.160 --> 19:13.027
But you'll get an A+ on the practical subject test,
which shouldn't affect the overall grades much.

19:14.120 --> 19:15.379
Um.

19:15.380 --> 19:18.440
It was stupid of me
to thank someone like you.

19:18.440 --> 19:20.280
No, you brought this on yourself.

19:20.280 --> 19:21.380
Are you joking?

19:21.580 --> 19:22.420
Well…

19:22.420 --> 19:25.160
Can you have her add her name now?

19:25.160 --> 19:26.260
Oh?

19:26.260 --> 19:30.120
Do you think I would give you
such valuable bargaining material for nothing?

19:30.120 --> 19:31.380
You are despicable.

19:31.600 --> 19:35.120
If you want to avoid failing,
then go do some of my work.

19:35.120 --> 19:36.760
I'm not going to ask you to kill someone.

19:37.000 --> 19:41.220
And the Katsuta Bread deal is over.

19:41.560 --> 19:42.732
Lastly,

19:42.733 --> 19:45.680
don't bring sauce
when you go into the ramen shop.

19:45.680 --> 19:47.603
You still remembered this?

19:48.820 --> 19:50.600
I had to do it.
It's all for the greater good.

19:50.600 --> 19:51.620
Wait, Miss Yuki.

19:51.620 --> 19:53.580
We can't yield to such threats.

19:59.980 --> 20:00.740
Hmm?

20:00.980 --> 20:02.000
Wind?

20:03.160 --> 20:03.710
Ah!

20:04.160 --> 20:05.720
NAME, YUKI YOKOYA
T-The name…

20:05.860 --> 20:07.100
Hey, hey!

20:07.100 --> 20:08.960
What did you do?

20:08.960 --> 20:09.880
No, just now…

20:09.880 --> 20:11.300
Hold on, Miss Yuki.

20:11.620 --> 20:14.319
She must have made a mistake, right?

20:14.320 --> 20:17.320
Or she saw a hallucination.

20:17.760 --> 20:20.260
Your name was on it from the beginning.

20:20.260 --> 20:22.820
You're quite smart now.

20:24.100 --> 20:25.440
I got it.

20:26.300 --> 20:28.320
I'll let you off the hook this time.

20:28.320 --> 20:29.760
It won't happen again.

20:29.760 --> 20:30.940
Sauce Junkie.

20:34.820 --> 20:37.500
It's not nice to say so,
but she's surprisingly easy to coax.

20:37.500 --> 20:38.840
I heard it, Hitoyoshi.

20:38.840 --> 20:39.980
Sorry.

20:42.780 --> 20:43.580
So,

20:44.060 --> 20:46.879
what exactly did you do, Miss Yuki?

20:46.880 --> 20:48.480
Well…

20:52.980 --> 20:56.900
This way, I've helped out Yuki, right?

20:57.260 --> 20:58.080
Yes.

20:58.400 --> 20:59.920
You've helped me a great deal.

21:00.320 --> 21:01.969
Thank you very much.

21:03.280 --> 21:03.960
Well…

21:03.960 --> 21:07.080
You are my classmate, right?

21:07.080 --> 21:09.280
Well…

21:09.760 --> 21:11.340
Hikage.

21:11.340 --> 21:12.499
Well…

21:12.500 --> 21:13.530
Well…

21:15.220 --> 21:17.151
Well, I…

21:20.100 --> 21:22.240
My name is Naka Hikage.

21:22.240 --> 21:25.400
Well, I have a way to win
at the Cultural Festival.
